\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee at 1-wk high but capped by firm oil   \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2007\par 04:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed to a near one-week high on Monday, as investors took positive signals from high-yielding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but concerns over firm oil prices and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:50 a.m. (0420 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.715/725 per dollar, moving up from 40.86/87 on Friday, and heading back towards a recent nine-year peak of 40.28 hit in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "The global cues suggest a stronger rupee, which is why we had such a strong opening, and the tone has been set for the day," said the chief dealer with a private bank who expects the rupee to trade in a 40.65-40.80 band on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Sentiment for the rupee was bolstered after high-yielding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose, a sign that investors were regaining appetite for relatively risky assets like the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought nearly $4 billion of local equities this year, after investing close to $8 billion in 2006. Still, concerns over firm oil prices weighed on the rupee. U.S. crude was trading near a nine-month high, after data last week showed stockpiles of the motor fuel in the United States unexpectedly failed to build.   \par \par \uc2 The prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the local unit also left dealers wary of building large positions in the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.06 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee in check in April, taking its total purchases to $24 billion for the six months from November. It is widely suspected of selling rupees over the past month to keep the dollar above 40.50 rupees.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070621e36i0004t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
