\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee steady with all eyes on flows, cbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2007\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was steady on Friday with traders caught between expectations of investment flows into the robust economy, and concerns about suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the local unit's gains.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:15 a.m. (0345 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.95/96 per dollar, a tad weaker than Thursday's close of 40.94/95. The rupee hit a nine-year peak of 40.28 in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  around, there's not going to be much of a downside for dollar-rupee," said a dealer with a state-run bank, who expects the rupee to trade in a 40.82-98 range on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rise has been powered by strong capital inflows, which have helped the the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  become the best performing Asian unit against the dollar this year.   \par \par \uc2 Large inflows could result in the overvaluation of the rupee and erode competitiveness of traditional and goods sectors in the long term, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rakesh Mohan said in a paper for a Bank of France seminar in Paris on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.06 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, taking the total purchases to $24 billion for the six months from November. It is widely suspected of selling rupees over the past month to keep the dollar above 40.50 rupees.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they would closely watch inflation data that will be released around noon (0630 GMT) for clues about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming weeks.   \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll showed \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual inflation rate at 4.80 percent for the 12 months to June 2, which would be the lowest annual rise since end of July last year.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that lower inflation gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupee's rise.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070618e36f0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
