\par\par \b \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $2.06 bln in April   \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 14:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.06 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, lower than the $2.3 billion it purchased in March, the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) monthly bulletin showed on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> began a sharp rally around mid-March and kept the momentum through April, hitting a nine-year high of 40.60 per dollar during that month.   \par \par \uc2 It has since risen to a fresh nine-year high of 40.28 in late May, but has slipped since then, and on Monday it ended at 40.80, up about 8.5 percent in 2007 making it Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 April's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the RBI's dollar purchases to $24 billion since the start of November 2006. It bought a record $11.9 billion in February to check the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of $26.8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fiscal year that ended on March 31. It had not purchased dollars between May and October in 2006/07.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's gains have been powered by robust capital inflows. Foreign funds have bought about $4 billion of local equities this year, after pouring in nearly $8 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI is widely believed to have sold rupees, though less aggressively in May and June, though traders remain wary of pushing the rupee much higher on fears of provoking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' wrath.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $205 billion on June 1, rising $28.2 billion in 2007. Traders said a large part of this year's increase was due to the RBI's dollar purchases.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $8.14 billion in 2005/06, down from $20.85 billion in the year before.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SNI|ABX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070611e36b00109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
