\par\par \b \uc2 Top dealer sees rupee up at 39 vs US dollar   \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 09:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee will continue to rise against the U.S. dollar this year, powered by massive investment flows into the fast-growing economy, though bouts of weakness are likely, a senior dealer with  \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of steam left in the rupee, we have seen a lot of flows, a lot of people overseas are interested and the interest is definitely going up," Rohan Lasrado, head for interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 He saw the rupee rising to 39 per dollar by end 2007. The rupee has gained nearly 8 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, making it Asia's best performing unit. Foreign funds have poured in about $4 billion into local equities this year, after investing nearly $8 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely suspected of acting decisively to cap the rupee's gains.   \par \par \uc2 Lasrado said that though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to persist, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) could allow a gradual appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has tried pushing it up and they know they fail on occasion, because when they push it up they see a lot of arbitrage and hedge funds and everyone who has not sold (dollars) comes in and sells," said Lasrado.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $22 billion in the five months to March in a bid to check the rupee and was widely seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to keep the exchange rate with the dollar above 40.50.   \par \par \uc2 The level of "40.50 is going to be a strong barrier for the moment because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is there protecting it, but very soon they will give it away, because a lot of flows are lined up from what we are seeing, and big flows," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Many medium and small-sized Indian exporters and importers remained unhedged, but sharp movements in the rupee would compel them to mitigate their risks, said Lasrado.   \par \par \uc2 "That will change, because if the rupee continues to remain volatile, they will change their exposure and keep their positions hedged. They will have to," he said.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 RUPEE-HDFC/|LANGEN|Table|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36b000je\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
