\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases to 1-wk low tracking weak stocks   \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2007\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, June 7 (Reuters) - The rupee tested a fresh one-week low on Thursday after a drop in stocks spurred investors to pare positions in the Indian unit amid concerns that a reversal in global risk appetite could prompt a wave of capital outflows.   \par \par \uc2  Traders said state-run banks bought dollars on behalf of oil importers, which further weighed on the rupee. The chief dealer of a corporate also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars at around 40.62.   \par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.7350/7450 per dollar, easing from Wednesday's 40.65/66, and moving further away from last week's nine-year high of 40.28.   \par \par \uc2  "The market's a bit jittery at the moment, and it's mainly the fall in stocks which is hurting sentiment," said the chief dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2  Indian shares fell 0.5 percent to their lowest close in three weeks as worries over the outlook for global markets and upcoming stock sales saw investors book profits on a two-month rally.   \par \par \uc2  Oil prices held firm above $71 a barrel, nearing their highest in nine months after a raid by Turkish troops into northern Iraq revived Middle East geopolitical tensions.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers remained cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $22 billion in the five months to end-March, and is widely suspected of being active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently, in a bid to cap the rupee.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee has risen over 8 percent so far in 2007, making it Asia's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year. It is up about 15 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July last year.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have poured $4.1 billion into local equities so far this year, after investing about $8 billion in 2006.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070610e3670001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
