\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Dubai trades world's first Indian rupee futures   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Summer Said   \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2007\par 01:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds Indian paper comment, session range, details)   \par \par \uc2  DUBAI, June 7 (Reuters) - A Dubai futures bourse began trading the world's first contracts on the Indian rupee on Thursday without the blessing of India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which may lose some control over the partially convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The Dubai Gold and Commodities Exchange (DGCX) said it launched the non-deliverable rupee-dollar contract to tap India's burgeoning foreign trade, especially with the United Arab Emirates, New Delhi's third largest trading partner.   \par \par \uc2  The DGCX, based in the UAE's commercial hub of Dubai, said it had discussed the contracts with the Reserve Bank of India, which bought $22 billion in the five months to March to check the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2  "They would not express an opinion one way or the other, which from our point of view is quite satisfactory," David Rutledge, a director at DGCX, told reporters in Dubai on Wednesday. "The market is outside the jurisdiction of India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which places curbs on trading in the rupee."   \par \par \uc2  India's Financial Express said the launch of the contract stemmed from what it described as Indian policy shortcomings.   \par \par \uc2  "Rupee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures trading on the DGCX in the Gulf emirate symbolises the profound mistakes of Indian economic policy," it said.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been convertible on the current account since 1994, meaning it can be changed freely into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for purposes such as trade-related expenses. It cannot be converted freely for activities such as acquiring overseas assets.   \par \par \uc2  "With the introduction of rupee futures, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also become slightly ineffective," said Srinivas Sribashyam, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at  \uc2 Bank Muscat International\uc2 , in Oman.   \par \par \uc2  "They will be keenly watching the Dubai rupee futures and it will be another source of frustration for the RBI," he said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SILENT   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility, declined to comment.   \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they like it really ... I don't think they can do anything about it," A.V. Rajwade, a member of an official panel on capital account convertibility, said in New Delhi.   \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -appointed panel has recommended a plan to allow fuller rupee convertibility and greater movement of capital in rupees by the end of the 2010/11 fiscal year.   \par \par \uc2  Rupee futures were likely to be a preferred hedging and investment mechanism against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations over the existing non-deliverable dollar/rupee forward market (NDF), some analysts say.   \par \par \uc2  "NDF has counterparty risk exposures and in futures contract traded on exchange there are no counterparty exposure risks because of the margining system," Rajwade said.   \par \par \uc2  "Having a platform that provides price discovery of the rupee will actually enhance the NDF market by making those contracts easier to price," said Ben Floyd, general manager of business and product development at DGCX.   \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed around 9 percent this year on increased capital flows as Asia's fourth-biggest economy expanded at the fastest pace in almost two decades.   \par \par \uc2  DGCX rupee trading focused on the key June contract <DIRM7>.   \par \par \uc2  Settlement price for 100 Indian rupees was $2.4583, with 645 lots having been traded. It hit a high of $2.4615 and a low of 2.4571 during the 12-hour session.   \par \par \uc2  "The volume is very good and it is more than what everyone in the market had expected, perhaps far beyond what RBI itself had expected," said a Dubai-based trader.   \par \par \uc2  Each non-deliverable rupee-dollar contract represents 2 million Indian rupees ($49,360). The maximum price fluctuation is $2 per contract which will be offered in the current calendar month and the following two, the DGCX said.   \par \par \uc2  In case of physical settlement, the euro-equivalent of the settlement price will be calculated, it said.  ($1=40.52 rupees)       \par \par \uc2 DUBAI-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|GFN|SNI|SNS|ABX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070607e367001q9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
