\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges past 40.50, mkt wary of cbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 4 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee headed towards last week's nine-year high on Monday, spurred by capital inflows and positive cues from most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers trod carefully on fears of provoking \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A trader with a private bank said two oil companies bought dollars in early trading, which kept a lid on the local unit, and the market was also watching for signs of dollar buying by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI), which is widely suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to block the rupee over the past two weeks.   \par \par \uc2 "We've broken the 40.50 mark today -- whether the RBI allows it to be broken decisively is the question on everyone's mind," said a dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. (0415 GMT) , the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.477/487 per dollar, up from Friday's finish    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 40.5450/5500. It hit 40.28 early last week -- its strongest\par level since May 1998 -- but was quickly pushed back to 40.50 by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought $22 billion in the five months to end-March to check the rupee's gains, and traders suspect it purchased about $800 million in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBI will sell 50 billion rupees of Market Stabilisation Scheme (MSS) bonds this week. MSS bonds are used to soak up cash from the banking system, including funds injected by its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With inflation trending downwards, analysts say the RBI has more elbow room to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index, the most commonly watched price barometer, rose 5.06 percent in the 12 months to May 19, the smallest annual rise in nearly 10 months, data showed on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee is Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar this year. It has gained about 9 percent, driven largely by strong capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070607e364000e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
