\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises but faces resistance at 40.50   \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2007\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee inched towards a recent a nine-year high on Friday as traders anticipated a burst of capital inflows into local equities, but was blocked again by state-run banks which bought dollars.   \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.540/547 per dollar, moving up from Thursday's 40.61/62. On Monday it hit 40.28 -- its strongest since May 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "The market tried to test the 40.50 level in the morning, but did not get through once again, which has been the story over the last few weeks," said the chief dealer of a foreign bank, who expects the rupee to trade in a 40.50-40.60 range on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that as soon as the rupee approached 40.50, state runs banks stepped up dollar buying, perhaps at the behest of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that is widely suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to cap the local unit.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility and maintain exporters' competitiveness.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top software services exporter,  \uc2 Tata Consultancy Services Ltd.\uc2  , said on Thursday that the rising rupee was hurting margins.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is Asia's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year, gaining about 9 percent on strong capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $22 billion in the five months to March-end, and is estimated to have spent about $800 million this week alone through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Still, dealers expect the rupee's rally to continue, with a wave of capital inflows slated for local equities and several IPOs, including a $2.4 billion issue by developer  \uc2 DLF Ltd.\uc2  that opens for subscription June 11-14.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070604e3610004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
