\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges up, but cbank in the way-dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2007\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, June 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee traded in a narrow range on Friday, caught between strong capital inflows and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening past 40.50 per dollar, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.5450/5500, up from Thursday's 40.61/62. On Monday it hit 40.28, its strongest level since May 1998.   \par \par \uc2  "The RBI was buying dollars at 40.52, protecting the level it has been for weeks, and the market was happy to keep selling to it today," said a dealer with a foreign bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The RBI is thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excess volatility and maintain exporters' competitiveness. It bought $22 billion in the five months to March-end in a bid to cap the rupee.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee is Asia's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year. It has gained about 9 percent, driven largely by strong capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   With exporters reporting the rupee's gains were denting\par profits -- top software services exporter,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Consultancy\par Services Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2          , said on Thursday that the rising rupee\par was hurting margins -- a growing section of the market believes\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Also, with inflation trending lower, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par more elbow room to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The wholesale price index rose 5.06 percent in the 12\par months to May 19, the smallest annual rise in nearly ten\par months, data showed on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "We believe the RBI will become more receptive to such\par (exporter) protests and more appreciation-adverse when\par inflation recedes," investment bank Calyon said in a note.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070604e3610004t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
