\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE1-India cbank:developing mkts will help manage flows   \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2007\par 05:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story issued late on Thursday)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 31 (Reuters) - India is moving towards a fully developed financial system to help it manage rising capital inflows, but needs to guard against risks arising from global imbalances, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Large capital inflows and the changing nature of tax collections had led to large volatility in cash levels in the money markets, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said had made its task of cash management more difficult.   \par \par \uc2 "Enhanced integration of financial markets allows risks to be shared more broadly and facilitates the flow of capital to the productive sectors," it said in its annual report on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance for the fiscal year 2005/06 (April/March).   \par \par \uc2 The report, though largely a historical document, does contain some forward-looking comments.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI has used market stabilisation scheme (MSS) notes and bonds to remove \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows of a long-term nature from the system, while its daily liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were intended to manage short-term fund levels.   \par \par \uc2 But a lack of knowledge of whether market inflows were long- or short-term funds made this difficult to judge properly.   \par \par \uc2 "There is, therefore, a need to explore further instruments/options to undertake liquidity management, particularly in the context of a move to fuller capital account convertibility," the report said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that there was also a limit on its MSS issuance, and it could not sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  indefinitely.   \par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web site, the outstanding balance under the MSS was 888.02 billion rupees as on May 18, below a self-imposed limit of 1.1 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said developing the financial system, which included the introduction of new products in the debt, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and derivative markets to help manage risks, would be a step towards fuller capital account convertibility.   \par \par \uc2 Other possible steps included allowing more investments by foreigners in the bond market and the launch of an instrument similar to federal fund futures in the United States.   \par \par \uc2 "Expansion of access by foreign investors to the Indian government securities market will have to be done carefully, taking into account issues related to opportunities for arbitrage, overall macro economic conditions and the need for financial stability," it said.   \par \par \uc2 The reforms of financial markets and the path to convertibility were linked processes, and were being managed in tandem, the report said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it had become more active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counter massive capital inflows, but the extent of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was relatively low when compared with emerging market economies.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee hit a nine-year high against the dollar earlier this week, largely driven by foreign inflows.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been effective in reducing the volatility in the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 While reaffirming its positive outlook on the economy, the RBI said that a global reversal in risk appetite could trigger a wave of capital outflows.   \par \par \uc2 "The re-pricing of risks can trigger massive adjustments in portfolio holdings of global investors and this can lead to sharp swings in capital flows out of riskier assets in emerging economies, with implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and other domestic financial segments," it said. The report will be posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web site:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbi.org.in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbi.org.in  }}}\par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/MARKETS (UPDATE 1) (RPT)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070601e3610005g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
