\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises tracking Asia but oil weighs   \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2007\par 05:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee inched towards a nine-year high on Tuesday as investors took cues from most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bet on a wave of capital inflows, but gains were limited by month-end dollar demand from oil refiners.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there were no large traces of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but if the rupee showed signs of rallying, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely step in to cap the local unit as it was widely suspected of doing on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> rupee was at    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 40.455/465 per dollar, off Monday's peak of 40.28 -- its\par highest level since May 1998 -- but stronger than the previous\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close of 40.51/52.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With 40.50 broken, it's going to be a slow grind ahead, with the market pushing the rupee higher and the RBI tempering the pace of appreciation," said the chief dealer of a private bank, who forecast the rupee would trade in a 40.40-40.60 range on Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the RBI bought about $600-$650 million after the rupee surged on Monday to a nine-year high on heavy dollar selling by a software services firm. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declined to comment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBI bought $22 billion in the five months to end-March trying to stem the rupee's rise, and dealers say it has played an active role in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in recent weeks.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee is Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar this year, gaining more than 9 percent on robust capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors have poured in nearly $3.7 billion into local equities this year, after investing nearly $8 billion last year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The 40.50 level was being held artificially by the RBI -- the real support for the dollar is around 40.20, and we should see some consolidation there," said a dealer with a foreign bank, who forecast the rupee would rise to 39.20 by August, boosted by strong inflows.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070601e35t0004n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
