\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee inches up, oil and cbank cap gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2007\par 05:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee inched up to a nine-year closing high on Tuesday, having spent most of the day caught between strong capital inflows and robust dollar demand from oil refiners to make month-end payments.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> rupee ended at 40.48/49 per dollar, up from the previous finish of 40.51/52 as it posted its strongest close since May 1998, but it stayed well clear of Monday's nine-year intra-day high of 40.28.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there were traces of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee touched 40.46, but said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying was relatively light compared to the estimated $600-$650 million it bought on Monday to drive the rupee from its peak.   \par \par \uc2 "It seems the RBI is still keen the rupee remains around the 40.50 level, but their resolve may start wearing down, because with the flows so strong the market will keep banging at the door," said a dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought $22 billion in the five months to end-March trying to stem the rupee's rise, and dealers say it has played an active role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks.   \par \par \uc2 Commerce Minister Kamal Nath said he expected foreign direct investment (FDI) equity flows of $30 billion in the fiscal year ending in March 2008, up from $15.7 billion in 2006/07, a comment many dealers took as a sign the RBI would gradually let the rupee rise.   \par \par \uc2 "This kind of comment helps the market feel more comfortable with the idea that the RBI will allow continued rupee strength, given it is based on more durable flows, as opposed to just portfolio flows," Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with  \uc2 ABN AMRO Bank\uc2  in Singapore, said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year, gaining more than 9 percent on strong capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070601e35t0004m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
