\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee off 9-yr peak as cbank steps in-traders   \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2007\par 04:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to afternoon)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, May 28 (Reuters) - The rupee rose to a nine-year peak on Monday, powered by strong inflows, but quickly gave up its gains as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying dollars aggressively to cap the Indian unit's rise.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk, but traders said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (RBI) presence drove the rupee down from an intraday peak of 40.28, its highest level since May 1998.   \par \par \uc2  At 12:15 p.m. (0645 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.55/56 per dollar. It closed last week at 40.59/595.   \par \par \uc2  "The RBI let the rupee appreciate for a while, but when they saw it rising too fast they came back and drove it down," said the chief dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking to smooth over excess volatility, he said.   \par \par \uc2  The RBI, which had bought $22 billion in the five months to end-March, started buying dollars aggressively at 40.30 on Monday in a bid to stem the rupee's rise, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  Lower inflation gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more elbow room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. Official data on Friday showed annual inflation eased to an eight-month low of 5.27 percent in mid-May.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee is Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, gaining over 9 percent against the dollar, driven higher by robust capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2  The market is expecting $4 to $5 billion of foreign money to flow into local equities by the end of June, including investments in an IPO by property developer  \uc2 DLF Ltd.\uc2 , that aims to raise a record $2.4 billion.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have bought more than $3.7 billion of local equities this year, after investing nearly $8 billion in the previous year.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070531e35s0004t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
