\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Off 9-Year Highs On RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Surge   \b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2007\par 14:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As at 1315 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           40.52      -0.07 \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   8.06%      -6BPS \par  Call Rate         6.00%      -100BPS \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  April             1.16       -0.25 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose Monday as strong local stocks spurred hopes of more foreign fund flows, but ended off nine-year highs as sustained \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped the unit's gains against the dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar breached a key INR40.50 level, slipping to an intraday low of INR40.28, a level last seen in May 1998.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at INR40.52 as against INR40.59 last close.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, with a dealer estimating the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $300 million-$400 million.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI has bought over $22 billion in the five months to March, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.   \par \par \uc2 "There was strong foreign fund inflows as well as non-deliverable forward market-related dollar sales by foreign banks. Some market estimates are putting inflows at $1 billion today," said a state-run bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the rupee rise in the initial session, but heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the dollar at INR40.30, he added.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee, however, may still have some strength as foreign fund inflows are expected to remain strong, but all eyes will be on the RBI, the dealer added.   \par \par \uc2 He expects the dollar to trade in an INR40.40-INR40.55 band in the coming session.   \par \par \uc2 "Going forward, the month of June is likely to see a huge amount of capital inflows, with a major initial public offering and two significantly large follow-up issues due. This would entail continued appreciation pressure on the rupee," said ICICI Bank in a recent note.   \par \par \uc2 Large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be needed to mop up these flows and may need a complimentary liquidity mop-up exercise, the bank said.   \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, prices ended higher as liquidity remained comfortable and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from issuing any bonds under its market stabilization scheme.   \par \par \uc2 Under the scheme, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mops up excess liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.07% 2017 bond closed at INR100.03 as against INR99.65 last close.   \par \par \uc2 "The absence of an MSS auction this week has really lifted the market," said a trader at a primary dealership.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market was fearing an INR50 billion-INR70 billion auction announcement over the weekend as around INR200 billion is being added to liquidity on account of redemption of 11.90% 2007 bond.   \par \par \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2 , in a note, said the absence of any fresh supplies of federal government papers in this week - the next scheduled auction for regular government borrowings is between June 1-8 amounting to INR80 billion - is expected to keep the benchmark 10-year yields on the lower side, though significant softening of the 10-year benchmark yields from the current levels of 8.06-8.08% is ruled out. "The 10-year paper yield faces resistance at 8.5% which it has not been able to breach. The price move has been too sharp since the auction cutoffs came in Friday," said a state-run bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 28-05-07 1254GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070528e35s000i6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
