\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Down On Fears Of Fresh Supply; Rupee Higher   \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2007\par 15:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As at 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           40.56      -0.03 \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   8.13%      +3BPs \par  Call Rate         7.75%      -5BPs \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  April             1.46       +0.05 . \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--India government bond prices fell Wednesday on fears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may issue more bonds to absorb liquidity created by its suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.07% 2017 bond closed at INR99.54 from Tuesday's finish of INR99.73. Its yield rose by 3 basis points to 8.13%.   \par \par \uc2 Market participants say the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to curb gains in the rupee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few session as the dollar fell to INR40.52 Monday, its lowest level against the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nine years. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI's suspected presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is adding to traders' fears," said the head of trading at a private bank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sell bonds worth INR50 billion next week under its market stabilization scheme to absorb the likely liquidity created."   \par \par \uc2 The RBI uses the MSS to suck excess liquidity out of the market by issuing bonds outside the federal government's regular issuance calendar.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said they also expected bond prices to remain subdued ahead of the federal government's INR80 billion bond auction Friday. The government is scheduled to auction INR50 billion of 7.38% bonds due 2015 and INR30B of 8.35% bonds due 2022.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupee ended marginally higher even though dealers were wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The dollar firmed to close at INR40.56 from Tuesday's finish of INR40.59.   \par \par \uc2 "Traders are wary of pushing the dollar-rupee below INR40.50-INR40.52 levels as we have continuously seen oil bids and talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels over the past two days," said Vikas Babu, a dealer at state-run  \uc2 Andhra Bank.\par \par \uc2 However, he said the rupee may soften in the coming sessions as foreign fund flows weaken over the weekend and on month-end dollar demand by oil companies.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar may rise to INR40.65-INR40.70 levels in the coming sessions," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Another dealer said that if the dollar breaches the INR40.53-INR40.55 support levels, the next support will kick in at INR40.40.   \par \par \uc2 -By Neelabh Chaturvedi and Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com . [ 23-05-07 1302GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070523e35n000qi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
