\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee blocked near 9-yr high by cbank-traders   \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2007\par 05:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee came within striking distance of a recent nine-year high on Wednesday, buoyed by capital inflows, but its path was blocked by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.550/565 per dollar, a shade higher than Tuesday's close of 40.560/570, and just off Monday's peak of 40.50 -- its highest since May 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI was was selling rupees around 40.53, but the question is for how long they can sustain this blocking," said a dealer with a private bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of India.   \par \par \uc2 "The flows are too strong, and there is a cost attached to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 The market is expecting $4 billion to $5 billion of foreign money to flow into Indian IPOs and equities by the end of June, which should add to the rupee's strength.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought $2.3 billion in March, in a bid to stem the rupee's rise, and dealers say it has been active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this week.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth excess volatility and to maintain exporters' competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  forecasts the RBI is likely to step up dollar buying, as slowing inflation gives it more elbow room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wholesale price index rose 5.44 percent in the 12 months to May 5, lower from the previous week's 5.66 percent, and falling within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target for the first time in five months   \par \par \uc2 "Accepting that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation was used as a tool to contain inflation, RBI could come back into the market to prevent sharp appreciation in the Indian unit once inflation cools," Kotak said on Wednesday, forecasting the rupee will weaken to around 41.10 by the middle of July.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070526e35n00041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
