\par\par \b \uc2 Cbank to knock Indian rupee off record highs-Kotak   \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2007\par 13:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 23 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to step up dollar buying in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and knock the rupee off a nine-year peak, as slowing inflation gives it more elbow room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,  \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has refrained from heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, allowing the rupee <INR=IN> to gain about 9 percent against the dollar so far in 2007, hitting a nine-year peak of 40.50 on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the RBI's hands-off approach was prompted by cash-fuelled inflation, which was further stoked by its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year.   \par \par \uc2 But, Kotak said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now overvalued by 16 percent and the nation's export growth was slowing, creating conditions for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to re-enter the market.   \par \par \uc2 This could drive the rupee down to about 41.10 by the middle of July, it said.   \par \par \uc2 "Accepting that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation was used as a tool to contain inflation, RBI could come back into the market to prevent sharp appreciations in the Indian unit once inflation cools off," Indranil Pan and Kaushik Das, economists at the bank, said.   \par \par \uc2 A temporary spike in the rupee in the near-term, however, could not be ruled out, they added.   \par \par \uc2 India's wholesale price index rose 5.44 percent in the 12 months to May 5, lower from the previous week's 5.66 percent, and falling within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target for the first time in five months.   \par \par \uc2 Concerned about a widening trade deficit and the potential for a sudden reversal of capital inflows, the RBI has kept the rupee in a broad range of 43.00-47.00 per dollar in the past three years.   \par \par \uc2 But strong economic growth and a booming stock market have attracted huge capital inflows, spurring the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $22 billion in the four months to end-March 2007, in a bid to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  expects the RBI to purchase $18.5 billion in the fiscal year ending in March 2008, in order to sustain annual GDP growth of 8.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/KOTAK|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070523e35n000ya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
