\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee in sight of 9-yr peak, cbank watched   \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2007\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed towards a recent nine-year high on Monday, as traders shrugged off tighter norms for companies to raise funds abroad and focused gains in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:40 a.m. (0410 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.600/615 per dollar, strengthening from Friday's 40.70/71. It hit a nine-year peak of 40.53 on May 9.   \par \par \uc2 "The market seems to have taken the tightening of capital controls in its stride, but people are still cautious about the RBI," said the chief dealer with a private bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since last November to stem the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 "But if someone takes a view that the RBI is not active, we may see a push towards 40.50," added the dealer.   \par \par \uc2 India tightened overseas borrowing rules on Friday, in a bid to curb capital inflows, which has caused the rupee to rise by nearly 9 percent this year, making it the best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would increase the yuan's trading band against the dollar from 0.3 percent to 0.5 percent, and raised interest rates, which also bolstered the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 News of the yuan's greater flexibility and the Chinese rate hike spurred Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firm against the dollar across the board on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Local traders said the gains by Asian units reduced the possibility of interevention by the RBI.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI, which is thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth over excess volatility and to maintain exporters' competitiveness, bought $2.3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, but analysts believe it has acted less aggressively in April and May.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070524e35l00055\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
