\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases as traders search for fresh cues   \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2007\par 05:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 17 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased against the dollar on Thursday, moving in a narrow band in lacklustre trade, as the market took a breather after a string of volatile sessions that kept the rupee in sight of a recent nine-year high.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they were wary of building large positions in either \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and were searching for cues on future direction.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.8550/8650 per dollar, slipping from Wednesday's close of 40.7800/7950, which was its strongest finish since May 1998, according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee hit a 9-year peak of 40.53 last week.   \par \par \uc2 "The market recently tried to take the rupee lower which didn't work, and now we've tried taking it higher but there's good resistance, so people are sitting tight for the time being," said the chief dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 The dealer forecast the rupee would appreciate by about one percent by the end of June, driven higher by strong inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained more than 8 percent against the dollar this year to be Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Traders said they saw strong dollar buying by state-run banks around 40.78, but the market did not have a conclusive view on whether it was at the behest of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI), which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to limit the rupee's gains.   \par \par \uc2 RBI deputy governor Rakesh Mohan said on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts were small relative to the turnover of the market.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, but analysts believe it has acted less aggressively in April and May.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070520e35h00064\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
