\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Mohan: RBI  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Low Vs Mkt Turnover   \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2007\par 11:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more details and bond prices)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is insignificant compared with the daily market turnover, the Reserve Bank of India's deputy governor said Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the volume (the size of RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is low compared to the overall turnover of the market," Rakesh Mohan said at a seminar on European financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 According to the latest data available, the RBI bought $2.31 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March, after mopping up a record $11.86 billion in February.   \par \par \uc2 The average daily turnover in India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is around $30 billion, market participants said.   \par \par \uc2 In the last financial year that ended March 31, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought around $27 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the rupee's gains against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupee has firmed up against the dollar in recent months largely due to robust foreign fund inflows.   \par \par \uc2 On May 7, the rupee hit INR40.53 to a dollar, its highest level in nine years. At 00830 GMT, it was trading at INR40.84 to a dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Change in SLR Depends on Monetary Conditions   \par \par \uc2 Mohan said the RBI will consider lowering banks' statutory liquidity ratio only after factoring in the underlying monetary conditions.   \par \par \uc2 Indian rules require banks to keep 25% of their deposits in approved bonds, gold or cash as statutory liquidity ratio.   \par \par \uc2 "The recent change in legislation enabled the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce the ratio, but depending of course on the macro and monetary conditions," Mohan said at the seminar.   \par \par \uc2 The federal government, which earlier had the power to change the statutory liquidity ratio, recently amended the rules to empower the RBI to decide on the floor of SLR.   \par \par \uc2 Bond prices fell after Mohan's comments on fears that any cut in the SLR will reduce banks' demand for bonds.   \par \par \uc2 Banks are the largest buyers of Indian government bonds.   \par \par \uc2 At 0830GMT, the benchmark 8.07% bond due in 2017 was trading at INR99.75, down from INR99.83 before Mohan's comments.   \par \par \uc2 "Though Mohan did not say that the SLR will be cut, the market just reacted to his statement as it needed one reason to sell after the rally (of last two sessions)," said a state-run bank's dealer, who didn't wish to be identified.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Neelabh Chaturvedi and Vipin V. Nair; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alpana Sarma [ 16-05-07 0920GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070516e35g000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
