\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Dn On Dollar Demand, RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Dn   \b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2007\par 15:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As at 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           41.28      +0.35 \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   8.12%      +4BPs \par  Call Rate         2.00%     -150BPs \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  April             1.71       -0.10 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee weakened Thursday on strong demand for dollars from importers and suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in the session.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at INR41.28, up from INR40.93 Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said exporters have stopped selling dollars at current levels and importers were now convinced that these were levels to buy.   \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the rupee's weakening was aggravated by rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the session.   \par \par \uc2 "There was buying again today by state-run banks in the later session like the past few days, which suggests a pattern. It is likely to be the RBI," said a dealer at a U.S. based bank.   \par \par \uc2 V. Rajagopal, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at  \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2 , said the trading pattern of the last two to three sessions suggested a rebound in the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "There is also a little bit of sentiment change from a feeling of further rupee appreciation to a little bit of doubt after the recent government statement on the rupee's rise," said Rajagopal.   \par \par \uc2 Federal Commerce and Industry Minister Kamal Nath Wednesday said the Indian rupee's gains against the dollar need to be halted.   \par \par \uc2 "We have taken it up within the government and my ministry has taken it up with the Reserve Bank of India," Nath said.   \par \par \uc2 Rajagopal expects some rupee bearishness to remain in the coming session and expects the dollar to trade in the INR41.15-INR41.40 range.   \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices fell as the market braced itself for fresh auction supply.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers are also speculating on the possibility of the RBI announcing a market stabilization scheme auction as the system continues to be flush with funds.   \par \par \uc2 The overnight cash rate fell as low as 2% on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's electronic dealing platform, compared with 6% normally seen at times of ample liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.07% 2017 bond closed at INR99.62 from INR99.92 last close.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is speculating that tomorrow the RBI will announce an MSS bond auction of around INR50 billion for next week," said a bond dealer at a state-run bank.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI is slated to sell INR60 billion of 7.49% 2017 bonds and INR40 billion of 8.33% 2036 bonds Friday, as part of its scheduled auction calendar.   \par \par \uc2 "Liquidity was comfortable so I feel prices fell probably as traders were selling bonds to buy the new securities at higher yields at the auction," said a private bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 She expects the yield cut-off on the 2017 paper to come in at 8.10%, but didn't offer any forecast for the longer-dated paper. .   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 10-05-07 1335GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070510e35a001de\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw1