\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges toward 9-yr peak; cbank watched   \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2007\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 8 (Reuters) - The rupee headed back towards a 9-year high on Tuesday, reclaiming some of the previous session's late losses as traders tested to see whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had decided to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:50 a.m. (0420 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.755/765 per dollar, up from Monday's close of 40.87/89.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee had hit 40.53 per dollar on Monday, its highest since May 1998, according to Reuters data, before skidding lower in late trade -- which some traders suspected was due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "There was panic when the rupee started falling yesterday, but sanity seems to have been restored, though I'm expecting a volatile session," said a dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "We'll be watching the stock market very closely for an indication about inflows," the trader added.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained more than 8 percent this year, with most of the gains coming in the last two months, boosted by capital inflows into the fast-growing economy. Foreign funds have bought more than $2.9 billion worth of stocks so far in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $19.7 billion in the four months to end-February in a bid to stem the rupee's rise, but is seen as having stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently.   \par \par \uc2 Helping the rupee was weakness in the dollar against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of three \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings this week that may underscore market expectations for U.S. interest rates to fall this year as rates in other major economies rise.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070511e35800074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
