\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee at 9-yr peak as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears ease   \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2007\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee struck a nine-year high against the dollar on Monday as investors felt confident that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit its gains, with sentiment also boosted by gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m (0430 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.595/605 per dollar, off an early peak of 40.53, its highest level since May 1998, according to Reuters data. It ended at 40.8450/8600 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI's body language suggests it's not concerned about the rupee's strength at the moment," said the chief dealer at a corporate, referring to the Reserve Bank of India.   \par \par \uc2 "If they don't, why should the market?" added the dealer, who said the dollar should find some support around the 40.50 level, as traders were likely to book profits.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained over 9 percent this year, boosted by robust capital inflows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $19.7 billion in the four months to end-February in a bid to stem the rupee's rise, but traders said it has not been a major presence in the market recently.   \par \par \uc2 The heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had increased money supply and added to price pressures at a time when the RBI was tightening policy to rein in credit growth and lower inflation -- which has led to the market belief that further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely for now.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee also found support after the dollar slipped against the yen and most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a soft payrolls report reinforced expectations the Federal Reserve would lower interest rates later this year.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070510e35700060\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
