\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Rise On Hopes of Lower Inflation, Rupee Gains   \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2007\par 15:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     As at 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           41.11      -0.07 \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   8.14%      -2 BPs \par  Call Rate         9.25%      +25BPs \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  April             1.96       -0.03 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--India government bond prices rose Thursday as traders bought securities on hopes that data due Friday will show inflation is falling, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Besides inflation data, dealers also expect a scheduled INR100 billion bond sale and a possible market stabilization scheme auction, which will determine the direction of bonds next week, they said.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.07% 2017 bond closed Thursday at INR99.46, up from INR99.32 at Monday's close. Its yield fell by two basis points to 8.14%. Indian financial markets were shut Tuesday and Wednesday due to local holidays.   \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing some buying in bonds as the market expects the latest inflation data to fall," said Piyush Wadhwa, treasury vice president at ICICI Securities.   \par \par \uc2 According to a Dow Jones Newswires poll of six analysts, wholesale price inflation for the week ended April 21 is forecast to fall to 5.86% from 6.09% in the week earlier period.   \par \par \uc2 The commerce ministry will release the data at 0630 GMT Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "Strong statutory liquidity ratio related demand from banks and a slight ease in liquidity conditions also aided bonds," said a dealer at a primary dealership.   \par \par \uc2 Under Indian law, banks have to maintain 25% of their deposits in the form of cash, gold, or approved securities, and report this position to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  every alternate Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The overnight call money rate eased marginally to 8.35% from 9.25% at Monday's close on the central's bank's electronic dealing platform due to a slight improvement in system liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee rose against the dollar on heavy dollar flows to the market.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at INR41.11, down from INR41.18 Monday close.   \par \par \uc2 "As the markets were closed for trading for the last two days, the accumulated dollar funds for the last few days came in to the system today," said a dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was also aided by strong foreign fund buying of local stocks, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's benchmark 30-stock Sensex rose 205.84 points, or 1.5%, to 14,078.21.   \par \par \uc2 However, the dealer at the private bank expects the rupee to weaken in the coming session on fears the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar could rise to about INR41.20 tomorrow as these bunched-up flows dry up and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The federal government has recently raised the ceiling for bond sales under the market stabilization scheme to INR1.1 trillion from INR950 billion previously, a move that will allow it greater flexibility in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 -By Neelabh Chaturvedi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com [ 03-05-07 1307GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070503e353000rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
