\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee recoups most losses as cbank stays away   \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2007\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 30 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee pared most of its losses on Monday as banks sold dollars in late trade and on relief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed out of the market, although it remained well clear of last week's nine-year highs.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 41.18/20 per dollar, off an intraday low of 41.445 but still weaker than Friday's close of 41.08/10. It hit a nine-year high of 40.60 last Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The Mumbai market will be shut for holidays on Tuesday and Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "A foreign bank sold huge amount of dollars on behalf of a big company," said a trader at a state-run bank.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee had fallen sharply in early trade on month-end dollar demand from oil importers and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought $19.7 billion in the four months to end-February trying to cap the rupee, and on Friday increased the issue limit to 1.1 trillion rupees for bonds it uses to absorb rupees released by its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 That move made traders wary that it wanted to rein in the rupee, which has risen by more than 7 percent so far this year, making it Asia's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 According to  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's trade-weighted index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by more than 15 percent, up from around 9.5 percent a month ago.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the bulk of dollar demand in the last few sessions had come from oil companies. Oil is India's biggest import, and U.S. oil <CLc1> was trading above $66 a barrel after Saudi Arabia said it had foiled a plot to attack its oil facilities.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070503e34u00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
