\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank raises ceiling on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bonds   \b0\par\par\uc2 By V. Ramakrishnan and Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with background, analyst reaction, bylines)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its firepower for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time in a week on Friday, raising the ceiling on the amount of bonds it can issue to absorb funds generated when it sells rupees for dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has appreciated more than 7.5 percent against the dollar since the start of the year, most of that in April, and hit a nine-year high of 40.60 per dollar <INR=IN> on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in a statement it was raising the 2007/08 ceiling for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds to 1.1 trillion rupees ($26.8 billion) from 950 billion rupees, and said it would review the limit again if the issuance topped 950 billion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 The outstanding balance for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, known as market stabilisation bonds, is now 780 billion rupees, it said.   \par \par \uc2 "Now the RBI has adequate ammunition for another round of dollar purchases keeping in view the strength of the rupee," said Indranil Pan, chief economist at  \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank.\par \par \uc2 The rupee closed at 41.08/10 per dollar on Friday. Its rise has been driven by large inflows of foreign investment capital as well as cheap debt raised abroad by Indian companies.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  extensively to try to curb its gains, buying almost $20 billion in the four months to the end of February, although traders say it possibly held off this month as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pumping inflation-fuelling cash into the domestic market.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI had only just raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond issue limit on Tuesday, when it took it to 950 billion from 800 billion, but the rupee has continued to appreciate and the market is nervous it could step in unexpectedly.   \par \par \uc2 But some analysts said Friday's move did not necessarily mean it was setting itself up for massive rupee-dampening action straight away - although it clearly was arming itself for more rupee selling at some point.   \par \par \uc2 "This only indicates that they are giving themselves extra elbow room for a future date, and they will watch incoming data such as money supply and bank loan growth before stepping in," said Manoj Rane, country treasurer at BNP Paribas \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "If they really wanted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  they would have caught the market by surprise, shown dollar bids in the market or even a verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have sufficed," he said.   \par \par \uc2 But the market might read the decision as an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  precursor and cut back short-dollar positions on Monday, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI is also concerned that annual credit growth, which has averaged 30 percent for the past three years, and money supply growth in excess of 20 percent, are fuelling inflation, which is hovering above 6 percent annually.   \par \par \uc2 It has tightened monetary policy aggressively since mid-December, although it opted to leave rates steady this week while it waited to see whether the measures were taking effect.   \par \par \uc2 One method of tightening has been to increase the cash reserve ratio -- the amount of funds banks have to keep with it on deposit -- a tool it has used three times since December. Many in the market expect it will raise the ratio further this year.   \par \par \uc2 "It tells you maybe more cash reserve ratio increases are not on the cards now and more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in store," said ICICI Securities analyst A. Prasanna.   \par \par \uc2 ($1=41.1 rupees). ((Writing by Charlotte Cooper, editing by John Mair; Reuters Messaging: saikat.chatterjee@reuters.com@reuters.net; Tel: +91-22 6636-9035))   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -BONDS/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070427e34r001ww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
