\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Indian rupee seen peaking at 40/dollar in 2007   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2007\par 15:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is likely to peak at 40.00 per dollar in 2007, although its current rally may be running out of steam after a rise of more than 8 percent this year, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The partially-convertible rupee hit a nine-year high of 40.60 per dollar <INR=IN> on Thursday, driven by foreign portfolio and direct investment as well as overseas fundraising by Indian firms, and is Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 The median forecast for the rupee among 11 economists surveyed was for a decline to 41.50 by the end of June and to 42.40 by the end of 2007, 4.4 percent above its close for 2006.   \par \par \uc2 But continuing strong capital inflows into the robustly growing economy were expected to propel the rupee to the psychological 40 level at some point this year and two economists forecast it would break through that barrier to 39.50.   \par \par \uc2 "The appreciation has been much faster than we expected. India is a fairly good bet among emerging economies due to its strong growth, high attractive yields and a hawkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Chin Loo Thio, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy to cool inflation via rupee appreciation will continue."   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) spent much of the past six months \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep rupee gains in check but since mid-March the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been rising and traders say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been scaled down substantially.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the reason is its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which pumped billions of rupees into circulation, was adding to cash-fuelled inflation pressures, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adopt a more hands-off approach.   \par \par \uc2 Annual inflation hit a two-year peak of 6.7 percent in early 2007 but has since cooled to about 6 percent and analysts expect a further retreat in headline numbers in the next two months. Once that happens, many see the RBI returning to its old \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  ways.   \par \par \uc2 "I think the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the inflation scenario clears out because this is a very, very sharp appreciation," said D.K. Joshi, chief economist at ratings agency Crisil.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key lending rate steady this week after five successive increases but it raised the limit on bonds it can sell to absorb funds generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , giving itself leeway to step in at a later date.   \par \par \uc2 "I see one more bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the inflows continue to be strong. The REER (a trade weighted) indicator is at unsustainable levels," Indranil Pan of  \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI's six-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  real effective exchange rate index stood at 112 in mid-April, showing the rupee was 12 percent overvalued.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's scorching run has forced a number of banks including  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 , BNP Paribas and  \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  to revise their rupee forecasts for the year.   \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 , a long-standing rupee bear, changed its year end forecast to 43 per dollar from 45.   \par \par \uc2 Forecasts by individual respondents for the rupee's dollar value at end June, end Dec and its peak in 2007 are as follows:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par  RESPONDENTS           END-JUNE       END-DEC             PEAK\par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par  ING VYSYA               42.13         41.88               39.5\par  KOTAK MAHINDRA BANK     42.75         42.75               40.5\par  ABN AMRO                43.0          42.0                40.0\par  JP MORGAN               41.0          43.0                40.0\par  STATE BANK OF INDORE    40.7          42.4                40.0\par   \f28 \uc2 \f2 RELIANCE INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2      41.5          41.0                N/A\par  CRISIL                  41.0          42.5                40.0\par  BANK OF BARODA          42.5          43.0                N/A\par  BNP PARIBAS             41.0          40.0                40.0\par  DEVELOPMENT CREDIT BANK 41.5          43.0                40.0\par  BARCLAYS CAPITAL        40.0          39.5                N/A\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par  MEDIAN                  41.5          42.4                40.0\par  AVERAGE                 41.6          41.9                40.0\par  HIGHEST                 40.0          39.5                39.5\par  LOWEST                  43.0          43.0                40.5\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Mumbai and Delhi Treasury) ((Editing by Charlotte Cooper; Reuters Messaging: saikat.chatterjee@reuters.com@reuters.net; Tel: +91-22 6636-9035))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/POLL|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070426e34q0022c\