\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips as traders see rally easing   \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2007\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped on Thursday as investors worried the momentum that took it to nine-year highs this week may be fading, but losses were limited as the dollar held near a record low against the euro.   \par \par \uc2 Concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also keep the rupee from testing Tuesday's high of 41.62 per dollar, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 At 10:45 a.m. (0515 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 42.160/185 per dollar, softening from Wednesday's close of 42.05/07.   \par \par \uc2 "After the rupee's rally earlier this week, the market's going through a bit of a correction, but nothing serious," said the chief dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is up 3 percent this month and is trading nearly 12 percent above a three-year low of 47.04 hit last July, bolstered by strong capital inflows into Asia's fourth-largest economy.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) is thought to have eased back on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb rupee gains in the past few weeks but traders say it may now be uncomfortable with the pace of appreciation, as a stronger local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dents exporters' competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought a record $11.9 billion in February in a bid to stem the rupee's rise. It bought $19.7 billion in the four months to the end of February.   \par \par \uc2 UBS cautioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was waiting for a clearer economic picture, and dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would resume if money supply growth and inflation eased.   \par \par \uc2 "We would therefore not be surprised if the RBI returns to the rupee market before the week is up," UBS said in a note.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070422e34j0001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
