\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee skids off 9-yr high on profit booking   \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2007\par 05:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 17 (Reuters) - The rupee skidded from fresh nine-year highs against the dollar on Tuesday, as investors squared off short dollar positions on fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stem the rupee's rally.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 41.97/98 per dollar, falling sharply from an intraday high of 41.62, its strongest since May 1998, according to Reuters data. It had ended at 41.85/86 on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "We might be heading into a consolidation phase, or for a bit of a correction," said Pradeep Khanna, director and head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, treasury and capital markets at HSBC India.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 12 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July, including more than 6 percent in 2007 to be Asia's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year.   \par \par \uc2 According to a JPMorgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by 14 percent, compared with 8 percent a month ago.   \par \par \uc2 A stronger rupee hurts the competitiveness of Indian exports, and the country's top software exporter  \uc2 Tata Consultancy Services\uc2  told Reuters on Tuesday that the rupee's strength was a major concern, and that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges worth $1 billion. Despite no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, traders remained concerned the rupee's recent strength may compel the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in coming sessions, in a bid to maintain exporters' competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee rose sharply in early trade, reflecting a squeeze on cash in the system, with overnight loan rates <INROND=> trading at around 16 percent, compared to 6 percent when cash is ample.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's gains have been fueled by domestic deposits by overseas Indians, that increased by $4 billion in 2006/07 while foreign borrowings by companies rose $14 billion, according to JPMorgan. Foreigners have bought more than $2.1 billion worth of shares so far in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Data from Venture Intelligence showed that private equity firms invested $2.5 billion in India in the first quarter of 2007, up from $1.27 billion a year earlier.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070417e34h0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
