\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee rises to highest vs dlr since Nov 1998   \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2007\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, April 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose on Monday to its strongest level against the dollar since November 1998, propelled by robust capital inflows, and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not yet \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its gains.   \par \par \uc2  At 10:45 a.m. (0515 GMT) the partially convertible rupee    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par <INR=IN> was at 42.30 per dollar -- a level last tested in\par November 1998, according to Reuters data -- compared with\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 42.51/52 at the previous close.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "There has been some good inflows over the weekend.\par Moreover the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has kept away from the markets and\par that is also boosting sentiment," said a trader at a foreign\par bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The Indian rupee, Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far\par this year, has gained for three consecutive quarters. It has\par risen by 11 percent since a three-year low of 47.04 in July,\par including a 4.5 percent rise so far in 2007.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Big capital inflows are posing challenges to financial\par authorities in emerging economies as they have to tighten\par policy to contain market volatility, but any increase in rates\par could in turn attract more flows, Rakesh Mohan, deputy governor\par at Reserve Bank of India, said on Saturday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Non-residents' deposits in India increased by $4 billion in\par 2006/07 while external commercial borrowings rose $14 billion,\par JPMorgan said in a note on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose above $200 billion\par for the first time in early April, which analysts said\par reflected capital flows and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par has the fifth-biggest holdings of reserves in Asia.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In February, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had bought a record $11.9\par billion from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to try slow down the rupee's\par surge and help exports remain competitive.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070419e34g0004m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
