\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee eases on oil buying,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears   \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2007\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to fix format with no changes to text) (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee backed away from a test of 8-year highs on Thursday as oil refiners stepped up dollar purchases and on fears that foreign investors might pare holdings in local equities, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders also said the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  loomed large over the market, deterring the market from building long positions in the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:35 a.m (0405 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 42.90/91 per dollar, easing from the previous close of 42.8275/8375 and an eight-year peak of 42.76 hit on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "The market feels the RBI will come in anytime the rupee falls below 42.80, so there's strong support for the dollar around those levels," said a dealer with a private bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of India.   \par \par \uc2 Data on Wednesday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $11.9 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in February. It was the fourth consecutive month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and stem the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee, Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in 2007, has gained for three quarters in a row and is up nearly 10 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to be uncomfortable with the rupee's pace of appreciation. Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain exporters' competitiveness, and also to smooth excess volatility.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that strong demand for dollars from oil companies on Thursday helped weaken the rupee. Oil is India's largest import.   \par \par \uc2 Traders also said the rupee was likely to come under pressure if investors pared their investments in equities, given weakness in U.S. and Japanese stock markets.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1, REPEAT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070415e34c00024\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
