\par\par \b \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $11.9 bln in Feb   \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2007\par 15:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 11 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $11.9 billion in February as it tried to rein in the rupee that rose to a 16-month high that month, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (RBI) monthly bulletin showed on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for the fourth month in a row, took dollar purchases to $19.7 billion since November. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure a stronger rupee does not hurt exports and to smoothen excess volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> closed at 42.8275/8375 a dollar on Wednesday, off an eight-year high of 42.76 hit on Monday. It has gained more than 3 percent in 2007, and is up nearly 10 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July.   \par \par \uc2 Traders were wary of building short positions in the dollar on fears of provoking \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although foreign capital inflows have been rising.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed to a record $199.2 billion on March 30. They rose $4.5 billion in March, and traders said part of this increase was due to the RBI's buying of dollars.   \par \par \uc2 In January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $2.8 billion after buying $1.82 billion the month before and $3.2 billion in November.   \par \par \uc2 Before that, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May, when it bought $504 million. It bought a net $8.14 billion in the financial year to March 2006, down from $20.85 billion in 2004/05.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070411e34b0013v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
