\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen losing steam, fall by June   \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2007\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 11 (Reuters) - India's rallying rupee, Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, should start losing momentum soon and head lower as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step in to ensure exports are not hurt, analysts said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN>, trading at 42.85 a dollar, has risen more than 3 percent since the end of December to its highest level in nearly eight years, thanks to a spike in interest rates and growing foreign investment.   \par \par \uc2 The biggest factor, however, for the rupee's climb has been the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which usually keeps a tight control on the unit through heavy market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 With its priority shifting to fighting stubbornly high inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed away from aggressively buying dollars against rupee sales -- because the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosts money supply and fuels inflation pressures.   \par \par \uc2 This could change.   \par \par \uc2 "In my view, inflation has probably peaked. When that shows marked signs of cooling, they will start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said Abheek Barua, chief economist at  \uc2 ABN AMRO Bank\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "I expect them to start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the second half of the month," he said, adding he expected the rupee at 43.50-44 by June.   \par \par \uc2 The annual inflation rate has slowed to 6.39 percent from a two-year high of 6.73 percent in early February, but is still above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort level 5-5.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its main lending rate five times in the fiscal year that ended in March, and increased the proportion of funds banks have to deposit with it three times in four months to douse inflation.   \par \par \uc2 There are concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again tighten policy when it meets on April 24.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the rupee's rise, of nearly 10 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July, has increased its overvaluation on a trade-weighted basis posing a threat to exports and a widening trade deficit.   \par \par \uc2 "The risk of a correction either via market forces or by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased," said Singapore-based Bank of America strategist Han-Sia Yeo, who expects the rupee to weaken to 44 by end-June.   \par \par \uc2 India's trade shortfall widened to $52 billion in April-December 2006 from $40 billion in the year-earlier period, and the stronger rupee is expected to squeeze margins of export-focused companies such as software services.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is currently overvalued by 11.1 percent against a basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of India's top trading partners, according to a JPMorgan index <JPMREER>, up from 8.1 percent a month ago.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is on the wrong side of the REER -- real effective exchange rate, privately maintained by the Reserve Bank of India, JPMorgan analysts Claudio Piron and Yen Ping Ho said in a note, raising concern that rupee "valuations have overshot".   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/OUTLOOK|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070411e34b000qi\par }\page {\par