\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee pulls back from steep fall; cbank eyed   \b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 30 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ran out of steam on Friday after partly recovering from its largest single-day percentage fall in nearly nine years, as investors shied away from testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve on the last trading day of the financial year.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> surged in early trade but ran out of momentum to end at 43.45/48 per dollar, recouping some of its losses from Thursday's close of 43.770/785 when it fell 1.7 percent on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 It had risen to 43.01 on Wednesday, its highest in more than seven years, Reuters data showed.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after market hours on Friday it was raising its short-term lending rate by 25 basis points to 7.75 percent with immediate effect and its cash resere ratio by half a percentage point, a move traders said would strengthen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "We should see dollars flow into the market as a result of the rate hike, which will push the rupee higher, though there should be good support for the dollar around 43.25-30," said the chief dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "What remains to be seen is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance. April may not have the strong inflows we saw in March, which will console the RBI, and perhaps they will keep their hands off," he added, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since November in a bid to thwart the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had risen by nearly $2 billion on March 23 from a week earlier, an indication of the extent to which it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is about 8 percent above a three-year low hit last July, and traders were wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be worried about its strength and want to cap further gains.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee was given a fillip after overnight rates soared to as high as 80 percent on Friday, their highest level in more than a decade, due to an acute shortage of funds as banks curbed lending to meet statutory capital adequacy requirements ahead of the financial year-end on March 31.   \par \par \uc2 Gains in the local unit were capped by strong demand for dollars from oil refiners for month-end payments. India imports about 70 percent of its oil.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070402e33u0005d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
