\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises past 43.50 to 19-mnth high  \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed past 43.50 versus the dollar on Wednesday to a 19-month high as traders dumped dollar holdings to take advantage of interbank rupee rates that rose as high as 70 percent on a cash crunch.  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 43.4450/4550 per dollar, its strongest close since Aug. 1, 2005, according to Reuters data, and taking gains over two days to 1.5 percent. It had closed at 43.85/86 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The cost of carry is heavy, which is keeping people from going long (dollars)... in fact (it) encourages people to go short," said Agam Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Standard Chartered Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We might visit 43.25 before it bounces back to 43.50/75. I think it will be (caused by) the combination of a natural correction and a bit of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is suspected of having sold rupees regularly since November in a bid to preserve exporters' competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight cash rate <INROND=>, the rate at which banks lend funds to each other, jumped to 70 percent on Wednesday -- which bankers said was the highest since 1996, when the rate topped 100 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Cash in the banking system shrunk sharply due to quarterly tax payments estimated at 300 billion rupees ($6.9 billion).  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month resumed bond sales under the market stabilisation scheme (MSS) after a gap of 18 months.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment was also lifted after the benchmark share index <.BSESN> rose 1.9 percent on Wednesday, raising expectations of further capital inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Still, traders were nervous the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to prevent the rupee from appreciating further and boost funds in a cash-starved system.  \par \par \uc2 Data shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased close to $8 billion in the three months to January, and traders widely believe it has played an active role in capping the rupee in February.  \par \par \uc2 "...the risks are high that the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to provide more liquidity and interrupt short dollar/long rupee carry plays that generate 2 bps a day carry," JP Morgan said in a note on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070324e33l00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
