\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee hits 19-mth high on cash shortage  \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to morning)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose to a 19-month high on Wednesday as traders sold dollars to raise funds to tide over a cash shortage that pushed interbank loan rates to their highest level in more than 10 years.  \par \par \uc2 Still, investors were watching for any sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the rupee's rise.  \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. the rupee <INR=IN> was at 43.710/720 per dollar, having hit a high of 43.65 in early trades, its strongest since August 2005. It had risen 0.6 percent to close at 43.85/86 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "It isn't some new India story that's driving the rupee up ... there's a large shortfall of rupees at the moment, and banks are selling dollars," said a dealer at a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The question is, how much the RBI will let the rupee move up?" added the dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight cash rate <INROND=>, the rate at which banks lend funds to each other, jumped to 70 percent on Wednesday -- which bankers said was the highest since 1996, when the rate topped 100 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The cash rate ended at 45-55 percent on Tuesday, compared with a rate of around 6 percent when cash is ample.  \par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts said the rupee's sharp gains may be temporary, and it could weaken as cash rates ease.  \par \par \uc2 "...the risks are high that the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to provide more liquidity and interrupt short dollar/long rupee carry plays that generate 2 bps a day carry," JP Morgan said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Data shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased close to $8 billion in the three months to January, and traders widely believe it has played an active role in capping the rupee in February.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070324e33l0001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
