\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee strengthens past 44/dlr to 18-mth high  \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 06:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to mid-morning)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, March 20 (Reuters) - Strong capital inflows powered the Indian rupee to an 18-month high against the dollar on Tuesday, but traders were keenly watching for any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  At noon (0630 GMT), the rupee was at 43.98/99 per dollar, having hit a high of 43.9225 per dollar, its strongest since late September 2005. It had closed at 44.11/12 on Friday, and the rupee market was shut on Monday for a holiday.  \par \par \uc2  "The rupee has gained mainly because the RBI is not there in the market, and strong inflows have pushed it higher," said the chief dealer at a private bank.  \par \par \uc2  The RBI has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since November to check the rupee's gains. Data shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased close to $8 billion in the three months to January, and traders widely believe it has played an active role in capping the rupee in February too.  \par \par \uc2  The rupee tested 44.03 per dollar last month.  \par \par \uc2  "I expect the RBI to come in soon, but when they will enter is anybody's guess," said the dealer.  \par \par \uc2  Sentiment on the rupee was buoyed on Tuesday after a global rally in equity markets steadied Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an indication that investors were regaining their appetite for risky assets.  \par \par \uc2  India's main share index <.BSESN> was up about 1 percent on Tuesday, which raised expectations of renewed capital inflows into Asia's fourth-largest economy.  \par \par \uc2  Foreign fund investments in India have helped the rupee gain about 6.5 percent from a three-year low hit last July.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070323e33k000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
