\par\par \b \uc2 TRADE IDEA-HSBC says buy Indian rupee  \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, March 12 (Reuters) - HSBC has recommended to buy the Indian rupee <INR=IN> as a jump in foreign direct investment (FDI) in recent months has calmed concerns of funding the country's widening trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2  The rupee could rise to 43 per dollar by the end of 2007, a level it hasn't tested since late-July 2005, the London-based investment bank said in a note to clients on Friday.  \par \par \uc2  The rupee was trading at 44.24 to the dollar on Monday.  \par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit of about $7 billion in July-September was offset by inflows of $9 billion, mainly from FDI and remittances by non-resident Indians.  \par \par \uc2  FDI inflows are expected at a record $12 billion in the current fiscal year ending on March 31, against $5.7 billion a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2  HSBC said \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the rupee to ensure exports are not hurt by a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may be forced to let the unit gain.  \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resist \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength and also face an overwhelming case for tighter monetary policy," it said.  \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed to a record $195 billion on March 2, up $14.6 billion from a month earlier, helped largely by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars to cool the rupee.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which involves selling rupees, has partly contributed to a spike in annual inflation to above 6 percent against a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  target of 5-5.5 percent by end-March.  \par \par \uc2  HSBC also said the rupee was not vulnerable to equity outflows as a recent stock market correction showed.  \par \par \uc2  "Indian rupee is not as highly leveraged to the equity market as the consensus believes. During the recent period, the rupee depreciated by just 1.1 percent and emerged again as one of the best performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said.      \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (TRADEIDEA)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070312e33c000ip\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
