\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee down on stock falls, weak Asia   \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 04:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped on Monday against the dollar, pulled down by weaker Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fears that a falling stock market would cause foreign investors to withdraw their funds.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:30 a.m. (0400 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.39/40 per dollar, down from Friday's close of 44.29/30 which was its weakest finish in over one month, according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2 "The negative sentiment that's pulling down stocks is spilling over into the (rupee) market," said a dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "But we don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  go through the floor either," added the dealer, who expects the rupee to trade in a 44.35-52 range on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The main share index <.BSESN> fell more than 3 percent in opening trades on Monday, extending last week's sharp fall.   \par \par \uc2 Stock markets elsewhere in Asia also fell again, with MSCI's index of Asian stocks outside Japan <.MSCIAPJ> down about 2.4 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The persistent weakness in Asian shares weighed on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the rupee, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Reserve Bank of India said it would use market stabilisation scheme (MSS) bonds to absorb excess cash from the banking system, which analysts believe could open the door for further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $193.1 billion on Feb. 23, a $4.2 billion increase from a week earlier which analysts said was an indication of the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the rupee.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by John Mair; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070308e335000ey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
