\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rangebound as traders search for cues   \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee traded in a narrow range on Thursday with investors circumspect after it fell in the previous session tracking weak global equities before getting support from suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, but they continued to be cautious after it was seen selling dollars on Wednesday when the rupee touched 44.37 to a dollar, its lowest level since Jan. 15.   \par \par \uc2 This came after months of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Indian unit.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 44.26/27 per dollar, a touch stronger than Wednesday's 44.27/28.   \par \par \uc2 "That's why they called the rupee a managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- the day you would think it will fly off it doesn't, and the day you think it will crash it doesn't," said a dealer at a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has been giving the market its rhythm," he added, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth excess volatility and protect exporters' competitiveness, but some analysts said it might also be to rein in money supply growth, currently running at 21.3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds pulled out $225 million from local equities on Monday and Tuesday, in line with a sell-off in global markets, official data showed, which weighed on sentiment.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the Indian share index <.BSESN> recovered a provisional 1.7 percent on Thursday after falling 4 percent on Wednesday, as fears of the impact of new tax measures eased, which helped buoy expectations for renewed capital flows into Asia's fourth-largest economy.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by Mark Williams; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070304e3310001c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
