\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee steady, traders cautious about stocks   \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was rangebound on Thursday as traders searched for fresh cues, though fears of capital outflows from the local equities that fell 4 percent in the previous session loomed over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 Traders keenly watched the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was seen selling dollars on Wednesday to halt the rupee's slide. This came after months of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Indian unit.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:30 a.m. (0400 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.27/28 per dollar. It had ended at the same point on Wednesday, but off an intraday low of 44.37, its weakest level since Jan. 15.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effort to prevent the rupee from free-falling yesterday was expected to some extent. Their stated policy is to control volatility, and it would have been hard for them to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  go on budget day," said a dealer at a private bank, referring to India's federal budget that was delivered on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "But with global markets settling down, I expect things to be a little calmer today," added the dealer who expects the rupee to trade in a 44.22-30 range on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth excess volatility and protect exporters' competitiveness, but some analysts said it might also be to rein in money supply growth, currently running at 21.3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds pulled out $225 million from local equities on Monday and Tuesday, in line with a sell-off in global markets, official data showed on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Indian share index <.BSESN> fell 4.01 percent on Wednesday to its lowest close in four months, dragged down by the global stocks slide and a budget that raised levies on some cement and widened the tax net for software services.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by Ranjit Gangadharan; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070304e3310001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
