\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases on oil demand; watching yen   \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2007\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Wednesday as oil importers bought dollars to meet month-end payments, and traders were watching the yen's gyrations after the Bank of Japan raised interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 At 11:05 a.m. (0535 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.19/20 per dollar, a touch weaker than Tuesday's close of 44.182/190, and slipping further from a 16-month high of 44.03 hit on Feb. 9.   \par \par \uc2 "With good dollar buying by oil companies today, there's been no need for the RBI (Reserve Bank of India) to jump in yet, but if the level moves below 44.18, we're expecting to see them again," said the chief dealer at a foreign bank, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rupee's strength.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by about $5 billion on Feb. 9 from a week earlier, which analysts said was an indication of the extent to which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said oil companies were actively buying dollars to meet overseas payments, which weighed on the rupee. Oil is India's largest import.   \par \par \uc2 Oil prices <CLc1> fell for a third day and were trading below $59 per barrel after forecasts that U.S. weather would moderate in March, bringing a likely end to an exceptionally mild winter season for the world's top consumer.   \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen had strengthened on reports the Bank of Japan would raise rates, and initially extended its gain after rates were increased.   \par \par \uc2 But then the yen weakened and local traders were expected to let it find a level against the dollar before making any large adjustments to their positions    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by John Mair; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070224e32l0002j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
