\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips as market wary of cbank stance  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2007\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped against the dollar on Tuesday, with traders wary of building up holdings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to block its attempts to strengthen beyond 44 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 44.150/160 per dollar, slipping from Monday's close of 44.135/140.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders believe the Reserve Bank of India has actively stopped the rupee from strengthening to 16-month highs past 44.  \par \par \uc2 "It's likely to be a lacklustre day: with the RBI's presence hanging over, the market is not comfortable doing large transactions," said a dealer at a foreign bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of India.  \par \par \uc2 "I expect the rupee to trade in a 44.12-17 range today," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Data shows that the RBI bought about $5 billion in November and December, and the market widely believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  consistently this year to check the rupee's gains and keep Indian exports competitive.  \par \par \uc2 JP Morgan estimates the RBI bought about $3.5 billion in the first half of February to weaken the Indian unit.  \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by about $5 billion on Feb. 9 from a week earlier, and analysts believe this was largely because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Robust foreign investment into \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped boost the rupee by about 6.5 percent from a three-year low last July, and the market thinks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is uneasy with the rupee's pace of appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Traders are also waiting on a Bank of Japan policy meeting that ends on Wednesday, with players divided over whether it will lift rates to a decade-high of 0.5 percent from 0.25 percent.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by John Mair; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070223e32k0005x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
