\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hovers near 16-mth high, cbank eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2007\par 04:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hovered near a recent 16-month high on Monday as banks sold dollars to meet funding requirements after a monetary tightening measure took effect over the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Only the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept a lid on the rupee's gains, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:10 a.m. (0440 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 44.07/08 per dollar, inching toward a 16-month high of 44.03 hit earlier this month, and up from the previous close of 44.10/11. The U.S. and many Asian markets are shut on Monday for local holidays.  \par \par \uc2 "We're expecting muted market conditions today. The market is waiting for fresh triggers," said a dealer at a private bank, who expects the rupee to trade in a 44.05-10 range on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "Call rates are tightening after the CRR (cash reserve ratio) hike, and the dollar is on the backfoot globally -- both positive signs for the rupee."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the reserve requirement that banks must hold with it to 6 percent of banks' deposits from 5.5 percent last week, a move that is expected to absorb $3.2 billion rupees. The first phase took effect on Saturday and the second will is on March 3.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee also found support after the dollar stayed at a near six-week low against the euro and a five-week trough versus the yen after a U.S. government report showed on Friday the pace of home construction fell 14.3 percent in January, fuelling expectations for a Fed interest rate cut.  \par \par \uc2 Reports of two bomb blasts that killed at least 64 passengers aboard a train travelling between New Delhi and the northern Pakistani city of Lahore around midnight on Sunday, had little impact on the rupee, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 But sentiment for the Indian unit was tempered by the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently bought dollars to ensure exports are not hurt by a strengthening domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It bought about $5 billion dollars in November and December, official data showed, and the market widely believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has played an active role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year.  \par \par \uc2 According to JP Morgan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $3.5 billion in the first half of February to weaken the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by Ranjit Gangadharan; Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070222e32j0006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
