\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hovers near recent peak, cbank watched  \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2007\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee held close to a recent 16-month high against the dollar on Monday, garnering support from renewed capital inflows, but the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed on sentiment, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:43 a.m. (0513 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.1350/1400 per dollar, barely changed from the previous session's close of 44.1325/1375. On Friday, the rupee hit 44.03 -- and was quoted at 44.00 -- its highest since September 2005 on a report in the Economic Times newspaper that the government wanted a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "The (capital) flows are strong, so the rupee will strengthen -- but just how much will depend on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a chief dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems to be a strong economic rationale behind a stronger rupee, but the RBI seems to have its own view," he added, referring to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) to limit the rupee's gains.  \par \par \uc2 Data shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $5 billion to weaken the Indian unit in November and December, and the market widely believes the RBI has played an active role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned about the rate at which the rupee has appreciated. It is about 6.5 percent up since hitting a three-year low in July.  \par \par \uc2 A stronger rupee dents Indian exporters' competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 But the prospect of robust capital inflows into Asia's fourth-largest economy boosted sentiment for the rupee, briefly giving it an early lift. Foreign funds have invested a net of $640 million into India equities in February.  \par \par \uc2 Still, traders expect dollar demand from oil firms to check the rupee's gains. U.S. oil <CLc1> traded above $59 per barrel on Monday. India imports about 70 percent of its oil.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070215e32c000kz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
