\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases on dlr demand from oil cos, yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2007\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 8 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Thursday tracking the Japanese yen's weakness against the dollar and as oil importers bought the U.S. unit aggressively.  \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the partially convertible rupee   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par <INR=IN> was at 44.13/14 per dollar -- further retreating from\par Friday's one-year peak of 44.05 -- and weaker than Wednesday's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close of 44.11/12.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Oil companies find these levels attractive, and came in strong today," said the chief dealer with a private bank. Crude prices <CLc1> hovered around $58 a barrel.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market also knows the RBI is defending the 44 level, and that it won't let the rupee strengthen further too quickly," he added, referring to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Reserve Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the Indian unit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee came under pressure in early trade after the yen slipped against the dollar as doubts mounted whether the G7 nations will issue a statement on the weakness in the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when they meet Feb. 9-10.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders also said they were wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought around $5 billion in November and December to cap the rupee, though some analysts think it would want to avoid adding to money supply and fuelling credit growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the rupees it sells add to money supply -- which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said is growing faster than it would like. Money supply growth has been one of the factors stoking inflation, which hit a two-year high in January.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I doubt they are \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a big way, because clearly their priority at the moment is liquidity management even if that means that the rupee appreciates," an economist at a foreign bank said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't let the rupee just go either. They are still going to target volatility."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee has risen about 6.5 percent since hitting a three-year low in July.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -  ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by Ranjit Gangadharan;\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070211e3280001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
