\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank checks rupee ahead of 1-yr high-traders  \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2007\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ran out of steam just short of a one-year high against the dollar to end steady on Wednesday, and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains had once again been thwarted by Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 44.11/12   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar -- after hitting an intra-day high of 44.07, in\par sight of Friday's one-year peak of 44.05 -- unchanged from\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday's close.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The RBI is protecting the spot rupee, and won't allow it to rise to 44 immediately," said a dealer at a private bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They may be hoping to hold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  till some natural market players take it to a lower plane. But ultimately they know that if the (capital) flows continue to be good the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will have to move to a realistic level - they just don't want the rise to be too rapid," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One fact that may attract more investment funds was the government forecast on Wednesday that the economy would grow 9.2 percent for the fiscal year ending in March, the fastest in 18 years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commerce and industry minister Kamal Nath told a panel of politicians on Tuesday evening that foreign direct investment could more than double to $12 billion in 2006/07.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by 9.2 percent, up from 8.3 percent a month earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A strengthening rupee dents exporters' profits, and the market suspects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buys dollars to preserve exporters' competitiveness and smooth over excessive volatility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showed the RBI bought around $5 billion in November and December to cap the rupee, though some analysts think it would want to avoid adding to money supply and fuelling credit growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the rupees it sells add to money supply -- which the RBI has said is growing faster than it would like. Money supply growth has been one of the factors stoking inflation, which hit a two-year high in January.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think the RBI is in vigilance mode, rather than market-correcting mode," said an economist a foreign bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Liquidity is their key goal, and keeping things tight is their objective. So massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not something they would be looking at."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -  ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by John Mair; Reuters\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070210e32700040\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
