\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee in sight of fresh 1-yr high; cbank eyed  \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2007\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee inched towards a fresh one-year high on Wednesday, tracking gains by most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, but the prospect of another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed on sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 At 10 a.m. (0430 GMT), the partially convertible rupee   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par <INR=IN> was at 44.07/08 -- in sight of Friday's one-year peak\par of 44.05 -- and stronger than Tuesday's close of 44.11/12.\par  "The only think holding the rupee down at the moment is the\par RBI... they are looking to stabilise the market. But with\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar weakening overseas they might allow a marginal appreciation of the rupee," said a dealer with a private bank, referring to the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the Indian unit's recent strength.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee was given a fillip after most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose against the dollar on expectations the yen's recent weakness may be discussed at this weekend's meeting of the Group of Seven finance ministers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet the market expects any sharp gains for the rupee to be thwarted by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is concerned at the rate at which it has appreciated: about 6.5 percent since hitting a three-year low in July.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A strengthening rupee dents exporters' competitiveness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought about $5 billion in November and December, and the market suspects that they have consistently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market this year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by 9.2 percent, up from 8.3 percent a month ago.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -                        MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -  ((Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, editing by Ranjit Gangadharan;\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters Messaging: cj.kurrien.reuters.com@reuters.net, 91-22-6636 9037))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070210e3270003z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
