\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Bonds End Lower Ahead Of Auction; Rupee Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2007\par 14:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           44.10       -0.01 \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.70%       +1bp \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   7.71%       +2bps \par  Call Rate*        7.65%       +15bps \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  January          INR1.30     -0.01 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     7.97%       -2bps \par  5-Year Mifor*     8.02%       -2bps \par  5-Year OIS*       7.64%       +3bps \par  \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are midpoints of bid-offer spreads. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices fell Monday as many market participants avoided big buying ahead of a fresh supply of paper Friday, although the market might pick up momentum in the next session, dealers said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The market is likely to be up tomorrow as liquidity has improved. Also banks' demand for bonds is likely to help the prices to recover," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The 8.07% 2017 bond ended at INR102.43 Monday, down from INR102.60 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "There wasn't much news today (Monday) to keep the market active. Also, there was some profit-booking taking place toward the closing," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The INR90 billion government bond auction Friday kept many players on the sidelines during the session.  \par \par \uc2 The government will sell INR60 billion of 7.37% 2014 bonds and INR30 billion of 8.33% 2036 bonds Friday as part of its market borrowing program for the current fiscal year that ends in March.  \par \par \uc2 HDFC Bank expects the yield on the 10-year bond to trade in a 7.65%-7.75% band during this week.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect the gilts market to be supported by the statutory liquidity ratio as well as investor (pension and insurance) fund buying...," the bank said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Indian rules mandate banks to keep 25% of their deposits in the form of gold, cash or approved securities as a statutory liquidity ratio.  \par \par \uc2 "The demand for SLR bonds should go up in the coming days as banks are now aggressively mobilizing deposits," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee ended nearly flat against the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from slipping further, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.10, as against Friday's finish of INR44.11.  \par \par \uc2 "The sentiment is still bullish on the rupee and the market will again take it upward," a foreign bank dealer said. "Foreign fund flows are continuing...It's the same India growth story."  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said he expected the dollar to test INR44.05 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 HDFC Bank expects the dollar to trade in a INR43.88-INR44.20 range during the current week as likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will moderate the pace of the rupee's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com [ 05-02-07 1323GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070205e325000qc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
