\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee lower on higher oil, cbank watched  \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2007\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Wednesday as global oil prices rallied, raising the prospect of more demand for dollars to buy oil, the country's largest import.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment was also weighed down by expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if strong capital flows pushed up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:05 a.m. (0435 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.265/270 per dollar, weaker than Tuesday's close of 44.24/25.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was active yesterday and the market is wary about getting caught on the wrong side," said the chief dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar demand from oil companies has weakened the rupee today, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stay away. It all depends on the flows," he added.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. oil <CLc1> hovered near $55 a barrel after rising 4.7 percent on Tuesday after U.S. officials announced plans to build up emergency crude reserves, and as colder weather in the world's largest economy pushed up demand.  \par \par \uc2 India imports about 70 percent of its oil and higher prices heighten the risk of widening the trade deficit, putting pressure on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said that expectations of capital inflows would limit the rupee's losses. Foreign funds invested a net of 71.7 million dollars on Monday, lending support to the Indian unit.  \par \par \uc2 Equity-related inflows have helped the rupee gain around 6.5 percent since it hit a three-year low in July.  \par \par \uc2 Yet, traders are wary of building up positions after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session weakened the rupee when it was around 44.20, a move widely viewed as a signal that it is uncomfortable with the rupee strengthening beyond that point.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also suspected of having bought dollars, through state-run banks, last week to weaken the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect exporters' competitiveness and curb excessive volatility, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Data last week showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $5 billion in November and December to check the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070127e31o0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
