\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee pare gains on suspected cbank hand  \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2007\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to afternoon)  \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The rupee pared gains on Friday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is worried about the impact of a stronger Indian unit on exports, traders said.  \par \par \uc2  At 3:45 p.m. (1015 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.27/28 against the dollar, off 44.25/26 but stronger than the previous close of 44.335/345.  \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state-run banks bought dollars at 44.26-44.28, probably for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in November buying $3.2 billion. The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) bank had also bought dollars on Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2  "They have been there intermittently. They seem to be protecting a particular level and keeping a tight leash on the rupee," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a foreign bank.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect export competitiveness and curb volatility in the rupee. A rising rupee in the past few months have hurt exporter margins and increased its overvaluation on a trade-weighted basis against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Software firm Satyam Computer Services Ltd.  lowered its revenue forecast for the year ending in March, citing a stronger rupee which reduces its income in rupee terms.  \par \par \uc2  Infosys Technologies  said the strengthening rupee shaved 200 basis points off its operating margins in October-December when the rupee gained nearly 4 percent.  \par \par \uc2  The rupee is overvalued by nearly 9 percent, higher than 7 percent from a month ago, according to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, which tracks the rupee on a daily basis.  \par \par \uc2  "This level of REER deviation has been associated with past RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and persistent  dollar bids from agent banks on Thursday appeared to have kept spot  supported over the session," said the investment bank in a note.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                  MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070122e31j00086\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
