\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Lower On Rumored RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2007\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           44.34       +0.14 \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.80%       +3bps \par  8.07% 2017 Bond   7.82%       +3bps \par  Call Rate*        7.80%      -20bps \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  December          INR1.27     -0.07 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     8.00%       -6bps \par  5-Year Mifor*     8.15%       -11bps \par  5-Year OIS*       7.67%       Unch \par  \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are midpoints of bid-offer spreads. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee ended lower Thursday amid rumored \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.34, as against INR44.20 at the last close.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee saw early gains on dollar selling by foreign banks, but subsequent buying by state-run banks, rumored to be on behalf of the Reserve Bank of India, stemmed the gains, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's decision to keep its overnight call rate unchanged at 0.25% also helped dollar sentiment, they added.  \par \par \uc2 "If the dollar-yen breaches 121.50, then we may see a dollar rally in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a foreign bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar-rupee is likely to trade in a 44.20-44.40 range in the near term with downside limited by possible RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I expect it to move toward 44.00-44.10 in a month's time," said V. Rajagopal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Kotak Mahindra Bank.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November and December, buying dollars to stem a rapidly rising rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought $3.20 billion in November and $1.82 billion in December, data showed.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that a U.K.-based bank was a major dollar seller on foreign fund related flows on a day when India's buoyant stock market ended on a fresh record high helped by strong corporate results.  \par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-stock Sensitive Index, or Sensex, gained 0.6% to close at 14,217.75.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, federal bonds ended lower as the market remained cagey ahead of a federal bond auction announcement and inflation data.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also speculated on the possibility of a cancellation of an upcoming auction as the federal government was flush with funds.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI is slated to sell INR50 billion 15-20 year bonds Jan. 18-Jan. 25.  \par \par \uc2 "The government has a sufficient balance with the RBI after the robust tax collections. Also, now investors don't have much appetite for bonds," said the head of bond trading at a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 The 7.59% 2016 bond closed at INR98.60 as against INR98.76 at the last close, while the 10-year 8.07% 2017 bond closed at INR101.67 as against INR101.90 last close.  \par \par \uc2 The market will also keenly await the inflation data Friday, due 0630 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Inflation is likely at 6.12% on the year in week ended Jan. 6, against 5.58% last week, according to a Dow Jones Newswires poll of five analysts.  \par \par \uc2 The estimate is way above the RBI's inflation estimate of 5-5.5% for the current financial year that ends March 31.  \par \par \uc2 However, Sujan Hajra, economist at Anand Rathi Securities said, "this week is an aberration and inflation will soften a bit in coming weeks due to the same base effect."  \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 18-01-07 1304GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070118e31i000nz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
