\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Frisky rupee sets monetary challenge to India c.bank  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anurag Joshi  \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2007\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 5 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to drain the banking system of excess cash to fight inflationary pressures, but the squeeze on funds has helped send the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an 11-month high.  \par \par \uc2 Now the market is wondering how much more rupee strength the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tolerate, especially as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would involve selling rupees into the market -- thereby adding more of that extra cash it is trying to drain out.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) says that when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it does so to calm rupee volatility.  \par \par \uc2 It steps in when foreign investment flows into the stock market, for example, drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up more rapidly than it likes, as when it was suspected of toppling the rupee from what was an eight-month peak of 44.35 per dollar <INR=IN> in November.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched 44.1250 on Jan. 2 with no sign from the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is now holding at about 44.30.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee has been an underperformer vis-a-vis other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Gaurav Kapur, senior economist with ABN Amro Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "You cannot stop the rupee's appreciation, given the kind of capital inflows we are witnessing. Chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are lower."  \par \par \uc2 Over 2005 and 2006, net foreign buying of Indian equities reached almost $19 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The RBI, concerned about 30 percent annual growth in credit fuelling inflationary pressures, raised its key lending rate four times last year and is now staging a two-part increase in the amount of cash banks are required to deposit with it.  \par \par \uc2 The first leg took place on Dec. 23 and the second is on Saturday. After the first one, the interbank overnight rate spiked 11 percentage points to 21 percent, the highest in nine years, although it has now come back to about 7.50 percent.  \par \par \uc2 As the rate went up, banks sold or swapped dollars to generate rupee funds, pushing the rupee higher.  \par \par \uc2 HANDS OFF, PERHAPS  \par \par \uc2 The RBI does not have an official target for the rupee, which has oscillated between 47.00 and 43.00 for the past three years.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gets uncomfortable when it estimates the rupee is overvalued by 8 to 10 percent on a trade-weighted basis -- especially when there is a rapid move to that level -- and that it is more prone to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check gains than curb losses.  \par \par \uc2 Some say that for now, though, with annual inflation near 5.5 percent, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will focus more on interest rates than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management and may tolerate greater rupee strength.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems to be some concern at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about overheating in the economy, particularly in certain sectors. Interest rate management, under such a scenario, is likely to take precedence over curbing rupee gains," Kapur said.  \par \par \uc2 "Technically, the next level to watch for is 44.02, with resistance at 44.65," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  letting the rupee gain, albeit gradually, with short bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check spikes.  \par \par \uc2 "We see the rupee at 44 per dollar by the end of March," said Sailesh Jha, senior economist with Credit Suisse in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 Others say the strength of capital flows into the stock market plus remittances and foreign direct investment may decide the extent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance.  \par \par \uc2 "They may not be comfortable with the sharp rise in the rupee. They may feel the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the export competitiveness," said Yes Bank chief economist Shubhada Rao.  \par \par \uc2 Others say cash conditions will not be so flush over the coming month. The increase in the cash reserve requirement has taken funds out of the system, says JPMorgan, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more leeway to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  without worrying unduly about the need to sterilise the rupee flows that result.  \par \par \uc2 If the rupee continues to appreciate in trade-weighted terms, as shown in JPMorgan's real effective exchange rate <JPMREER>, which suggests it is moving out of the comfort zone, then the RBI may cap it.  \par \par \uc2 "The RBI retains this option. They would look at how strong inflows are and how strong the pressure on the rupee to appreciate," JPMorgan economist Siddharth Mathur said.  \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|SNI  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070108e315000ow\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
