\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Remains At 10-Month High; Bonds Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2006\par 14:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           44.29       Unchanged \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.63%       +2 bps \par  Call Rate*        12.50%      Unchanged \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount \par  November          INR1.25     -INR0.02 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     7.89%       -17 bps \par  5-Year Mifor*     8.01%       -8 bps \par  5-Year OIS*       7.48%       +5 bps \par  \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are midpoints of bid-offer spreads.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee, which ended flat at its over 10-month high against the dollar Thursday, is likely to gain in the coming sessions as banks may continue to sell more dollars to tide over a current liquidity squeeze, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.29, its same closing level as Wednesday, and the lowest finish since Feb. 15.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar should test INR44.10-INR44.00 in the next 10 days," said a dealer at a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 The current liquidity crunch in the Indian banking system has spurred large-scale dollar selling by banks to get the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "As long as it is not a runaway appreciation for the rupee, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market (to support the dollar)," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Also, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not want to inject more rupee into the banking system through its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time when it seeks to absorb liquidity by raising banks' cash reserve ratio, or CRR, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India is increasing the CRR 50 basis points in two stages to absorb about INR135 billion from the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 The CRR rose 25 basis points to 5.25% from Dec.23, and will rise another 25 basis points from Jan.6.  \par \par \uc2 The CRR is the proportion of time and demand deposits a bank must hold in cash with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 This increase in the CRR, coupled with quarterly advance tax payments by Indian companies in December, has severely impacted liquidity, which pushed up the overnight call money rates to the current level of 12.50%.  \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices fell in thin trade Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.59% 2016 bond ended at INR99.70 from INR99.79 at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is absolutely lackluster. Unless the picture on liquidity changes, it is likely to remain like this," said a dealer with a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 The bond market will take fresh cues from the inflation data due at 0630 GMT Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 According to a Dow Jones Newswires poll of six analysts, the wholesale price index-based inflation for the week ended Dec. 16 is likely to be 5.39% on the year, from 5.32% a week before.  \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair, Dow Jones Newswires, 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 28-12-06 1312GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061228e2cs000f4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
