\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee climbs to 10-mth high on cash squeeze  \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2006\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 28 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee gained to its strongest against the dollar in 10 months on Thursday as banks sold dollars to meet funding needs amid a cash squeeze that has pushed the call money rate to six-year highs this week.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said capital inflows into local equities and the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the rupee had prompted some dealers to sell the dollar aggressively.  \par \par \uc2 At 4:30 p.m. (1100 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 45.27/28 per dollar after climbing as far as 44.22/44.23 -- its highest since mid-February, according to Reuters data. It ended at 44.30/31 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The typical end-of-month importer demand seems to have abated for the moment. Also capital inflows are strong and that is pushing the rupee higher," said R.K. Gurumurthy, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ING Vysya Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have bought more than $8 billion of Indian equities this year. Further, the rupee's yield attraction had increased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would increase the cash reserve requirement (CRR) for local banks, which has tightened the supply of cash and pushed up market rates.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight money market rate hit 13 percent on Wednesday -- its highest since September 2000 and well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight lending rate of 7.25 percent -- and was around 12 to 12.5 percent on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "There was some concern the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupee's sharp rise but that hasn't happened so far, as that would blunt the CRR hike objective," said a senior trader at a foreign bank."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the rupee's export competitiveness against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or curb volatility. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also adds to the supply of rupees in the market, which effectively loosens monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 According to a JP Morgan index <JPMREER>, the rupee is overvalued by more than 8 percent compared to about 7 percent in the month-ago period.  \par \par \uc2 "Strong inflows supported by a largely optimistic sentiment towards emerging markets should push USD/INR lower, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb volatility and check valuations might result in limited upside for the rupee," said a recent JP Morgan report.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061231e2cs0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
