\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Rises To 10-Month High; Bonds Trade In Range  \b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2006\par 14:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           44.29       -0.16 \par  7.59% 2016 Bond   7.61%       -1 bps \par  Call Rate*        12.50%      +175 bps \par  \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount \par  November          INR1.27     -INR0.25 \par  \par  Interest Rate Swaps \par  2-Year Mifor*     8.06%       +7 bps \par  5-Year Mifor*     8.09%       Unchanged \par  5-Year OIS*       7.43%       -8 bps \par  \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are midpoints of bid-offer spreads.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose to more than a 10-month high against the dollar Wednesday and is likely to extend gains in the coming session as a severe liquidity crunch in the local banking system induces large-scale dollar selling, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "I expect the dollar to test INR44.00-INR44.10 any time now. It is very difficult to hold long-dollar positions in the current market conditions," a dealer at a private bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR44.29, its lowest finish since Feb.15, and down from INR44.45 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said that although the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , heavy dollar selling by foreign and local banks pushed up the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 "The RBI was there in the market, but it was not trying to push up the dollar. It was not aggressively buying (dollars)," a dealer at a state-run bank said.  \par \par \uc2 "All people who are short on the rupee are now selling dollars," the dealer said. Foreign fund flows into the local stock market is another factor that weakened the dollar, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Liquidity in the Indian banking system dwindled because of quarterly advance tax payments by Indian companies in December and a higher cash reserve rate imposed on banks by the RBI.  \par \par \uc2 In a bid to absorb about INR135 billion from the banking system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised the cash reserve ratio 50 basis points in two stages.  \par \par \uc2 The CRR rose 25 basis points to 5.25% from Dec. 23, and will rise a further 25 basis points from Jan. 6.  \par \par \uc2 The CRR is the proportion of time and demand deposits a bank must hold in cash with the RBI.  \par \par \uc2 The severe liquidity crunch in the market was evident from the jump in overnight call money rates, which surged to 12.50% Wednesday from 10.75% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The cash crunch also took its toll on the government bond market as trading volumes plunged Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.59% 2016 bond ended at INR99.79, compared with INR99.74 at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is holding at the current levels only because of banks' requirement to buy bonds to meet their SLR. Otherwise the prices would have fallen," said the head of bond trading at a private bank.  \par \par \uc2 Indian rules require banks to keep 25% of their deposits in gold, cash or approved securities as statutory liquidity ratio reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Bond market participants said they don't expect trading to pick up in the coming sessions unless banking system liquidity improves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 27-12-06 1313GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061227e2cr000f4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
