\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee inches up on liquidity dollar sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2006\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose slightly on Wednesday as traders sold dollars amid a cash crunch in the banking system, but expectations of month-end demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from oil companies checked further gains.  \par \par \uc2 Liquidity in the banking system has been tight over the past week due to quarterly corporate tax payments.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's weakness against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a recovery in Asian units following a U-turn by Thai authorities on measures to slow the rise of baht also underpinned the rupee's strength.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> ended at 44.7150/7250 per dollar, compared with the previous close of 44.745/755. It was wedged in a narrow range between 44.6850 and 44.75 during the day.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it is likely to stay that way for the rest of the month. Christmas week should be very quiet," a trader with a private sector bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said inflows into Indian equities are likely to continue in the first half of 2007 as the U.S. market was showing signs of slowdown, which in turn could boost the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares closed 0.31 percent down on Wednesday on tepid inflows from institutional investors and some profit-booking.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is up more than 5 percent from a three-year low of 47.04 in July on strong foreign fund inflows, which have topped $8.4 billion this year.  \par \par \uc2 It hit a near-eight month high of 44.35 on Nov. 10 but strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled it down.  \par \par \uc2 The market largely shrugged off \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's November trade data, which showed that the deficit had widened to $6.20 billion in November from $3.87 billion a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The trade gap widened to $36.04 billion in the first eight months of the fiscal year that began in April, from $29.06 billion in the same period last year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061223e2ck0001o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
